[
  Quantix(
    id: "69fa1c933ad81a99cecc92b2",
    fact: "Wood Frogs Survive Being Frozen Solid During The Arctic Winter",
    shortDescription: "Wood frogs stop their hearts and freeze completely solid to survive harsh winters in the frozen north woods.",
    longDescription: "Deep in the Arctic, the wood frog survives conditions that would kill almost any other vertebrate. As temperatures plummet, these amphibians allow their own blood and tissues to freeze, effectively stopping their heart and breathing for weeks at a time. To prevent cellular damage from ice crystals, they flood their bloodstream with a natural antifreeze made of glucose and urea. This high concentration of sugar acts as a biological cryoprotectant, keeping their vital organs intact while the rest of their body turns into a literal frog-shaped popsicle. Once spring arrives, the ice melts, their heart restarts, and they simply hop away, having successfully cheated death through complex chemistry.",
