    fact: "Giant Underground Rivers Flow Beneath The Amazon Rainforest Canopy Floor",
    shortDescription: "Immense subterranean rivers transport more water than the Amazon River itself through porous rock deep underground.",
    longDescription: "Deep beneath the lush surface of the Amazon rainforest lies a hidden hydrological giant known as the Hamza River. Stretching four thousand kilometers from the Andes to the Atlantic, this massive aquifer flows through porous sedimentary rock at a sluggish pace of mere millimeters per year. Unlike the surface river that rushes toward the ocean, this subterranean behemoth remains trapped in darkness, moving vertically through the crust before turning horizontal. Discovered by researchers analyzing heat data from retired oil wells, this geological anomaly proves that the true scale of the Amazon Basin's water cycle extends far deeper into the Earth's crust than any satellite or explorer could ever observe from the surface.",
