    shortDescription: "A teaspoon of neutron star material weighs as much as the entire human population of Earth combined today.",
    longDescription: "When a massive star exhausts its nuclear fuel, it undergoes a cataclysmic collapse, crushing its core into a sphere only twenty kilometers wide. This remnant, known as a neutron star, packs the mass of our Sun into a volume no larger than a city. The resulting density is so extreme that protons and electrons are fused into neutrons, creating a superfluid core. If you were to scoop up a mere teaspoon of this exotic matter, the gravitational force would be so intense that the substance would instantly plummet through the Earth's crust, tearing through the planet to settle at its core, leaving a trail of destruction in its wake.",
