    fact: "Gallium metal melts instantly when held in a human hand.",
    shortDescription: "Gallium is a soft metal that transforms from a solid to a liquid at just 29.7 degrees Celsius.",
    longDescription: "Gallium is a fascinating metallic element that defies the common expectation that all metals are hard and rigid at room temperature. With a melting point of only 29.7 degrees Celsius, just slightly below human body temperature, a solid chunk of gallium will begin to liquefy the moment you hold it in your palm. This process is not a chemical reaction but a physical phase change triggered by your body's thermal energy. When it cools, it reverts to a beautiful, crystalline solid. This unique property makes gallium a popular element in science demonstrations, as it provides a tangible, real-world look at how atomic lattices respond to heat, making the invisible world of thermodynamics visible to the naked eye.",
