    shortDescription: "Stomach acid is so powerful it can dissolve razor blades while the lining protects the organ itself.",
    longDescription: "The human stomach contains hydrochloric acid with a pH level between one and three. This extreme acidity is essential for breaking down complex proteins and neutralizing harmful bacteria ingested with food. To prevent the stomach from digesting itself, the organ is coated in a thick layer of protective mucus and rapidly regenerates its own lining cells every few days. This robust defense mechanism is so efficient that the stomach can withstand corrosive substances capable of dissolving various metals. While the stomach is incredibly resilient, it requires this specific chemical environment to initiate digestion, proving that our internal physiological processes involve intense, controlled chemical reactions that maintain our survival every single day.",
